W: 1. As we marched down to Fennario
W: As we marched down to Fennario
W: Our captain fell in love with a lady like a dove
W: They called her by name pretty Peggy-o
W:
W: 2. What will your mother think, pretty Peggy-o?
W: What will your mother think, pretty Peggy-o?
W: What will your mother think when she hears the guineas clink
W: The soldiers all marchin' before you-o?
W:
W: 3. In a carriage you will ride, pretty Peggy-o
W: In a carriage you will ride, pretty Peggy-o
W: In a carriage you will ride, with your true love by your side
W: As fair as any maiden in the ar-ee-o
W:
W: 4. Come skippin' down the stairs, pretty Peggy-o
W: Come skippin' down the stairs, pretty Peggy-o
W: Come skippin' down the stairs combin' back your yellow hair
W: And bid farewell to sweet William-o
W:
W: 5. Sweet William is dead, pretty Peggy-o
W: Sweet William is dead, pretty Peggy-o
W: Sweet William is dead and he died for a maid
W: The fairest maid in the ar-ee-o
W:
W: 6. If ever I return, pretty Peggy-o
W: If ever I return, pretty Peggy-o
W: If ever I return, all your cities I will burn
W: Destroying all the ladies in the ar-ee-o
